The env_0077 earned-wage-access scenario is finished and delivered in `env/env_0077_earned_wage_access_provider/`. All three delivery conditions hold. Every difficulty passes the source-layer audit with both tasks PASS and the charter clean. Every one passes the KB-layer audit with no open items. `validate_scenario` returns VALID.

**What was built**
- **Company:** Paystride, Inc., an employer-integrated earned wage access and payroll card provider, with its card accounts at a partner bank. Employers and hourly workers are both customers.
- **Products:** 7 in all. Five are claimed by a difficulty (program agreement, payroll card program funding, instant pay disbursements, worker access plan, worker payroll card). Two are unclaimed (Save and the payroll-repaid loan).
- **Tasks:** 5 difficulties with 2 tasks each, 10 in total. Each task is a chain of prerequisite problems ending in an act only the customer can perform, such as signing a termination notice, sending their own wire or ACH transfer, requesting their own early wage transfer, or signing a written card-dispute claim.
- **Documents:** 309 KB documents (program 55, paycard 47, disburse 59, access 57, card 59, save 16, loan 16). Every product passes `check_docs`.

**Final checks, re-run by me rather than taken from subagent reports**
- All 7 instantiation gates print OK for every difficulty.
- After publication, `check_traceability` is OK for all five difficulties.
- The blueprint files are byte-identical to the hashes taken when the blueprint was frozen.
- No customer ID, name, phone, email or tax-ID digits are shared across difficulties.

**How hard each difficulty was to close**

| Difficulty | Source-audit rounds | KB-audit rounds |
|---|---|---|
| paycard | 1 | 3 |
| disburse | 4 | 2 |
| program | 6 | 4 |
| access | 8 | 3 |
| card | 9 | 2 |

Each KB audit was finally judged with every product published, so no cross-product figure was left unconfirmed. The run took about 18 hours and survived four account-limit cuts.

**Calls I made that you may want to review** (all are in `worklog.md`):
- **Blueprint defects left in place:**
  - Some eligibility checks in the blueprint (program amendments, termination and closure roles) can never be satisfied by the solvability gate. The program difficulty dropped its planned amendment task because of this. The paycard and disburse difficulties worked around it with declared, scoped replacements.
  - The Save and loan renderers reported 14 wording defects in their base text, such as a parameter name left inside rule text and a contradictory downgrade-grace description.

  Neither changes any scored answer, so the frozen blueprint was not edited and these texts are published as they stand.
- **Card disputes:** no record links a lost/stolen card report to a particular loss. So the card dispute schedule only prices claims on accounts with at most one lost and one stolen card replacement in the last 12 months. Accounts with repeated losses are referred to Paystride's fraud review team, and the schedule books nothing for them. The auditor accepted this.
- **Program late charges:** a shortfall notice with less than 25.00 open carries no late charge. This stops a charge from rounding to 0.00 while another charge waits on it.
- **Points I did not send back for rework:**
  - Six employer payment rows in one program task fall on weekends or holidays. No rule sets dates for employer payments.
  - In paycard task 0, two adjustments cancel out exactly. An agent that misses both still lands on the correct fee. The audit passed it because each adjustment changes the answer on its own.

I also saved a memory note with the new failure patterns from this run, so later runs can brief against them up front.
